      "writtenOn": "2023-08-18T09:03:52Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "So if the default network is null we\u0027re going to kill live TCP sockets ?\n\nI\u0027m not sure how it makes sense to use the default network for this at all. The point here is to save battery by not waking up the modem right ?\n\nIn the old code, putting an app in the freezer will kill all its live sockets (whether on the default network, some local network, some non-default network, anything). That is simple and it makes sense.\n\nBut in the new code, we immediately destroy sockets on the cell network when the app is put into the freezer iff the default is wifi ? It will wake up the modem and I do not understand how that makes sense.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 3015,
        "startChar": 16,
        "endLine": 3015,
        "endChar": 37
      },
      "revId": "40ff361bee02cb230a6ef272e8d633164ae4b4d1",
